  "applies_to": "Produal RTX-D room transmitters with display (temperature, humidity, CO2, VOC, light; outputs and configurable buttons), application software 2.1.9.7.",
  "summary": "RTX-D is a room transmitter/controller with display that measures temperature, humidity, CO2, VOC and light, and has external inputs, four outputs and configurable buttons. It is a BACnet MS/TP B-ASC device. The PICS gives 65 objects: measurements, calculated values (dew point, enthalpy and so on), BMS-written controller inputs, setpoints and output values, button states and timers.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "2.1.9.7",
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": true,
  "notes": [
    "Taken from the PICS value-range tables (ID, object name, values, resolution, units, default). The PICS has no read/write column; objects named BUS-... and SETPOINT-... are taken as BMS-writable, the rest as read-only.",
    "Temperature objects report in °C or °F depending on the unit setting.",
    "Binary input and binary value objects are supported by type but none are listed in the PICS.",
    "MS/TP baud rates 9600 to 115200 bit/s.",
    "Shares many names and IDs with the older RT/RTX map (for example OUTPUT1-VOLTAGE = AV 13) but adds external input 2, light, button and outdoor/setpoint objects."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BACnet protocol implementation conformance statement, RTX-D (published 02.02.2026)",
    "doc_number": "EN - 53011WD0B0PICS",
